  "note": "The trusted composition gains withheldReopen {register, reopen}: a one-use capability names a retained native transaction by operation, wallet lane and hash, with the job owner's private pass context, and reopen runs the lease, confirmation and broadcast of those retained bytes once when the whole dispatch history shows no possible transmission. It reuses the transport's rule for what never sent the bytes (UNSENT_STATES and nothingSent, moved unchanged to native-dispatch-history.mjs), and it treats lane and intent rows at broadcast-started, or finished as withheld at the last check, as holding no broadcast answer. A withheld broadcast still goes on through a new lease as before; the reopen also reaches one whose rows a failed write left at broadcast-started. The held transport facade, the wallet and a relay carry no reopen. On the buyer side only the explicit recheck that names a suspended effect route signs a fresh proof of the resume, bound to its own request, and only the seller clients that call builds can send it, once, on its first attempt. The fee checks, the explicit wallet broadcast and the withheld finish of the lane are unchanged."
